    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate prioritizing stolen base upside and favorable platoon splits to compensate for a tight cap environment. **Corbin Carroll** is our clear headliner with an Elite score of 77.76; he benefits significantly from a soft matchup against Pallante and a slow opposing delivery that creates a high-probability environment for him to exploit the basepaths. Similarly, **Brice Turang** (68.63) and **Jose Caballero** (66.13) project as high-ceiling plays today. **Turang**\u2019s move to the #3 hole provides essential RBI protection, while **Caballero** is a critical leverage play against Valdez; despite hitting #8, his dynamic platoon advantage against the lefty and the favorable delivery metrics make him a more efficient start than many of our mid-tier options. **Kyle Karros** also cracks the 60 threshold, bolstered by an extreme park factor (+14%) that forces his inclusion despite the lower batting order position.\n\nOur most difficult decision revolved around the bottom of the outfield, where **James Wood** (52.60) was edged out of a more prominent role by the efficiency of our speed-first strategy. While **Wood** carries an elite xwOBA of .402, he faces a tough tactical hurdle in Mayza\u2019s elite 1.88s catcher pop time, which directly suppresses his stolen base projection. Consequently, the optimizer favored the stolen base environment surrounding **Caballero** and **Carroll**. Meanwhile, **Dalton Rushing**, **Travis Bazzana**, **Austin Riley**, and **Zach McKinstry** round out the active roster, though **Bazzana**\u2019s score is slightly dampened by the L/L matchup against Kay. We remain sidelined regarding **Vinnie Pasquantino**, who stays on the IL, while **Josh Naylor**, **Tyler Soderstrom**, and **Mickey Moniak** are excluded due to team off-days or confirmed benchings. We continue to monitor the status of **Giancarlo Stanton**, **Seiya Suzuki**, **Trevor Story**, **Gabriel Moreno**, **Max Muncy**, **Henry Bolte**, **Alex Freeland**, **Cole Young**, and **Carson Williams** for future spot starts, but for today, the focus remains on leveraging the speed of our active nine.",
